// operator tokens so that step-by-step computations are likely to be placed
// inside delimiters. Inside spans it uses parser-valid constrained decoding,
// with mild repetition avoidance and caller-supplied token-group preferences,
// and closes the span as soon as the parser reports completeness. This tracked
// state supports valid generation because parser authority is used exactly on
// the constrained segment, while delimiter/state transitions keep
// currentConstrainedOut synchronized with the visible text between delimiters.
