//   via EnterObservedConstrainedSpan/OpenConstrainedSpan, and [] is valid by the
//   precondition parser.IsValidPrefix([]). In the complete-prefix branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan exits constrained mode, so the implication becomes
//   vacuous. In the active constrained branch, each constrained-step helper
//   returns either EOS or a token preserving parser validity; on non-EOS we use
//   AppendConstrainedToken, which keeps currentConstrainedOut parser-valid.
// progress: In the unconstrained step branch, UnconstrainedStep consumes one
//   token-step and we append at most one visible token, so
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved after steps := steps+1.
//   In the forced-open branch, OpenConstrainedSpan consumes one token-step and
//   appends exactly the visible delimiter, again preserving the bound. In the
//   close branch, CloseConstrainedSpan consumes one token-step and appends at
//   most the close delimiter, so visible growth is at most the consumed budget.
//   In the constrained branch, the chosen helper consumes one token-step; EOS
//   may consume budget without visible growth, while AppendConstrainedToken adds
//   at most one visible token on non-EOS, so the output-length bound remains
//   true.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
